+# Agent workflow
+
+- Use `guest/gate.sh --focus MODULE --filter 'module::*'` while editing. The
+  default full gate is cached; use `guest/gate.sh --force` once for final fresh
+  acceptance. Preserve the command exit status; never infer success from a log.
+- Keep source inputs stable while a compiler job runs. The gate snapshots them
+  by content and rejects a changing copy. Do not share mutable `/tmp/v` trees.
+- Use the pinned `.mylang/current` installation. Change it only with
+  `tools/update-toolchain.sh PATH`, which validates and records a complete
+  compiler, QBE, LLVM adapter, and runtime installation.
+- Leave `MYLANG` unset for normal work so a paused shell cannot retain an old
+  mutable compiler path. Set it only for a deliberate toolchain experiment.
+- Use `guest/pcb.sh ...` or call the path printed by `guest/build-app.sh` for a
+  command matrix. It builds once per source/compiler identity. Preserve every
+  application argument. For probes, pass a private `--journal` directory.
+- Application builds use LLVM O3+LTO and at most two allowed CPUs by default.
+  Use `PCB_BUILD_MODE=debug` for LLVM O0 or a positive `PCB_BUILD_JOBS` to alter
+  the affinity bound. Do not route this workbench through QBE: its generated
+  extraction unit exceeds QBE's practical memory limit.
+- Start long gate/build calls with `run_in_background`. Rely on the completion
+  notice; use `job_output` with `wait: true` only when dependent work remains.
+  Do not sleep-poll jobs, output, or source arrival.
